From 8eaf3fc87a0fbc2fb5c1ca526ade76006c6929f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:54:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta: a single-game executable on the SDL frontend,
 without the Qt interface

ss-delta.exe boots Soul Sacrifice Delta (PCSA00152) straight into a plain
SDL window. The settings the game needs are fixed (Vulkan, high accuracy,
surface sync, double-buffered memory mapping); the player's choices come
from ss-delta.ini next to the executable, written with comments on first
start: paths, resolution and window scale, fullscreen, vsync, filter,
volume, recompiled modules on/off, log level, validation layer. The
recompiled modules (ssd_aot_*.dll) are found in the configured folder
unless SSD_AOT is set. Config and log live in ss-delta/ next to the exe;
the shader cache is shared with Vita3K.exe.

sdl-frontend gains two hooks: on_event (every event, before the session)
and on_tick (every loop pass). ss-delta uses them for F11/Alt+Enter and
a window title with the frame rate, in Vita3K's format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
